Z||000000||DJRice||01-25-2001||09:32 PM||||This is an email I got....I may actually start doing this.<P>The following was taken from this website: <A HREF="http://www.whoohoo.net/junkmail/," TARGET=_blank>http://www.whoohoo.net/junkmail/,</A> <BR>and pasted here so you don't have to listen to that annoying music. Its a great idea....<P>Tired of getting all those pre-approved letters in the mail for everything<BR>from credit cards to 2nd Mortgages, and junk like that?<P>If the answer is, "Yes!" read on.  If "No," read on anyway since many of us don't care for banks and credit card companies anyway.<P>As you know, most, if not all of those letters come with a  postage "PREPAID" envelope. Why not get rid of some of your other junk mail and put it in these cool little envelopes !<P>If you didn't get anything else that day, then just send them their application back! Just make sure your name isn't on anything you send them.<BR>Heck, you can send it back empty if you want. Keep 'em guessing that way.<P>Let's turn this into a chain reaction! Eventually, the banks and credit card companies will begin getting all their own crap back in the mail.<P>Let's let them know what it's like to get junk mail, and best of  all...<P>THEY'RE paying for it--Twice!    AND HERE'S THE BEST PART:<BR>You already know that the United States Postal Service has increased postage<BR>rates again, starting the first week of January 2001.<P>Now if all of us start mailing back all the junk mail we receive to other junk mailers in their 'postage paid' envelopes...we just might delay the next rate hike from the USPS for years and years to come!<P>Let the chain reaction begin, please send this to all your friends!<BR>||||reg||8
